CORE
main.cpp
--cpp17
^\[main\.assertion\.1\] line \d+ T is_constructible from S via operator T\(\): SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.2\] line \d+ S is_convertible to T via operator T\(\): SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.3\] line \d+ WRONG must FAIL: FAILURE$
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
^CONVERSION ERROR$
--
N5008 [over.match.copy]/1: converting to class type T from class type S
considers both T's converting constructors AND S's conversion functions.  The
trait path synthesises a declval<S>() operand (a class prvalue); binding it to a
source-side conversion function's `const S&` implicit object parameter failed
because reference_binding required the `this` receiver to be an lvalue or a
recognised temporary.  Per [class.mfct.non-static]/1-2, [over.match.funcs]/5 and
[class.temporary]/3 a class prvalue may be a member-call receiver via temporary
materialization; the synthetic source is now flagged so reference_binding
materializes it.  Non-vacuous: assertion 3 must FAIL.
